WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:07.670
Man, today's got to be the hottest one yet.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:11.520
Good morning, Master.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:12.680
Morning.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:18.120
Why are you wearing your uniform?

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.120
Oh, now that you mention it...

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.500
We hadn't noticed.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.120
You're still on summer break, aren't you?

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:26.000
How foolish of you.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:28.510
We have class today.

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:30.630
Oh, is that so?

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:36.890
But you know,
it somehow strengthens your image.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.710
You look more dignified than usual.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.890
You're just delusional.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:46.750
Don't be so reserved!

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:49.900
Of course, you still look best in a karate gi.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.600
Thanks for breakfast.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:30.870
So hot...

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:35.560
Good morning.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:36.790
Good morning!

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:38.470
Yo!

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:41.140
Water...

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.890
How undignified, Miyako.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:45.950
Good morning.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:47.440
Morning!

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:50.140
What's that?

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.150
Soothing curry bread.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:56.510
What's that supposed to mean?

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:58.320
Murasame-san?

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:01.960
The teacher wants to see you.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:03.240
Oh, okay.

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:14.020
Good morning.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.910
Those are some additional assignments and a survey. I need you to hand them out for me.

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:24.340
We have to submit our plans for the future already?

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:26.370
It's mainly to see how it goes.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:31.490
Well, it doesn't hurt to think about whether you want to work or go to college.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.930
I'll explain the details later.

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:39.300
Isn't it a bit cold?

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:45.910
Excuse me.

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:49.410
It's hot, isn't it?

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:57.920
I wish it would rain or something.

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.080
Close the windows.

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:29.180
Akemiya, would you turn on the lights?

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:30.200
Sure.

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:37.000
Well, that's how it is.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.810
Hand in the surveys after the break.

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:43.230
Make sure you put some thought into it.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:47.020
All right, you can go home
after you're done cleaning up.

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:52.370
Those of you who were going to clean outside,
help the indoor group.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.020
A veritable deluge.

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:00.860
Tomoe-chan, do you have an umbrella?

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:02.050
I don't.

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:04.900
Still, it shouldn't last long
if it's just a quick shower.

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:06.770
You two over there.

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:09.030
Make sure you clean like you're supposed to.

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:12.990
I'll give you a hand.

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:13.970
Thanks.

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:16.020
In that case,
could you get the other side?

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:16.290
Sure.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:23.800
Aoi-san, will you write another book?

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:28.440
Yeah. I'll write another
for Orino-sensei in the winter.

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:33.860
Aren't there any other authors you like?

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:35.900
Nope.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:37.060
I see.

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:39.310
I'll help you again then.

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:44.820
I'm sure you'll be busy too.

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:48.660
But if something comes up,
I might ask you for help.

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:51.830
All right. That sounds good.

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:04.340
Fools.

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:06.720
They'll obviously get wet.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:10.840
There are times when I envy the boys and their freedom.

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:15.290
How dreary.

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:17.730
The rain is subsiding.

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:20.100
It should clear up soon.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:22.630
Where should we eat on the way home?

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:24.520
The usual place is fine.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:26.240
Kaza— oh?

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:34.370
Oh my, is the pinecone going to ignite?

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:36.380
It's a "charred stake."

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:42.660
It's fine. She's already been rejected by her once.

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:46.140
Oh! Well, then you have nothing to worry about.

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:48.630
The way you put it vexes me somehow.

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:51.810
I'll put these back, then.

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:54.610
I'm sorry to trouble you
even though you're not on duty.

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:55.640
I don't mind.

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:03.020
Listen to this! Senpai's so cute.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:08.830
At the sushi restaurant, she misheard "thank you for your business" as "my darling."

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:12.790
Is that cute?

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:15.660
It appears to have made
an impression on Kazama-kun.

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:19.210
Ushio-chan, what would you like to eat later?

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:28.460
Thanks.

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:29.940
It's all right.

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:32.850
What a simpleton.

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:42.020
What is it, Miyako?

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:45.890
"That thing"?

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:48.740
Is it some kind of memo?

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:52.860
That's bad. They wrote in the book.

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:57.790
Senpai, could I borrow an eraser?

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:01.420
I wonder what "that thing" refers to.

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:04.920
Is it something people aren't supposed to see?

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:08.890
Doesn't it pique your interest, Murasame-kun?

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:13.310
I'm sure it's already been found.

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:14.550
Most likely.

00:08:15.310 --> 00:08:18.560
Nevertheless, it's possible that
the clues are still there.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:22.060
Either way, it'll be a good way to kill some time.

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:26.120
Well, I guess it's fine.

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:27.810
It's settled, then.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:30.430
Ladies of the Girls' Club!

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:34.320
We'll now commence with an extracurricular event.

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:40.950
That sounds kind of fun.

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:50.480
Ah, it's damp in here since it's been closed off.

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:56.840
Hey, what did that memo say again?

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:59.240
"Pull the lever, open it, and retrieve it."

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:00.140
Here.

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:05.850
Don't worry. I haven't used it yet.

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:08.360
Thank you.

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:11.470
Where is this lever?

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:16.280
Ah! It smells like Kazama!

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:18.620
Lame!

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.860
I wonder if this is it.

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:26.360
It's structurally impossible
to hide something here, though.

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:29.140
Is there another lever somewhere?

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:31.620
Ah, so that's what it is.

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:34.900
I thought it meant a more edible "liver."

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:39.300
It's not a barbecue restaurant.

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:53.320
Pull out the liver...

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:58.570
...open it, and retrieve it.

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:02.110
Well done, Torioi-kun.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:21.490
What are they doing?

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:25.590
So this is "that thing"?

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:30.280
More precisely, "that thing" might be hidden there.

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:33.480
Why do they have to be so cautious?

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:38.740
If you're secretive to the point that it's never found,
then there's no meaning to it.

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:39.740
Is there?

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:42.570
Well, it's good for us.

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:45.000
Still...

00:10:46.230 --> 00:10:48.700
The boys' locker room, huh?

00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:50.570
What should we do?

00:10:50.990 --> 00:10:55.170
The boys' locker room itself
is not a place to fear, but...

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:58.060
How should I put it?

00:10:58.060 --> 00:11:02.430
It's not a place fit for the Girls' Club.

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:05.250
It's probably all smelly and dirty!

00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:07.510
I don't want to go!

00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:09.310
Are we just going to give up, then?

00:11:09.970 --> 00:11:11.910
Well...

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:15.980
Is there no one who could retrieve it for us?

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:19.570
Don't you know any boys
we can use at a time like this?

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:22.820
What about you?
They're always flocking to you!

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:30.840
Rather than acquaintances, it would be more accurate to say that they exist to make me look better.

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:32.050
You're a cruel one.

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:34.330
What about you, Ushio-chan?

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:38.620
I'm sorry, but I don't really talk to boys.

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:41.630
That's just like you, Kazama-kun.

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:44.860
Still, it's too bad.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:47.350
I'm a bit curious about it myself.

00:11:49.970 --> 00:11:50.780
Oh!

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:54.370
Why me?

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:56.930
Who was that again?

00:11:56.930 --> 00:12:00.480
That's Akemiya-kun — the vice president.

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:04.110
I have a hard time remembering
the names and faces of boys.

00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:08.790
So Sumi-chan gets along with men too!

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:13.250
Just open it up and take it out quickly.

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:14.450
Please!

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:20.280
But that locker hasn't been
used by anyone for a long time.

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:22.640
What if they put something dangerous in it?

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:23.940
I don't know.

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:25.390
No way!

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:29.410
You're the only one we can rely on, Akemiya-kun.

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:31.770
It's your duty as a man. Please?

00:12:33.070 --> 00:12:34.040
A man?

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:39.180
I understand, Murasame-san. I will go!

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:46.550
We are most grateful for your assistance and sincerely hope for your survival.

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:50.310
Wait for me, Murasame-san.

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:52.640
Uh, sure...

00:12:57.530 --> 00:13:00.710
Murasame-san is counting on me.

00:13:01.940 --> 00:13:05.280
And this time, as a man!

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:10.420
When I leave this place behind,
I'll tell her how I feel again.

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:14.780
Not as a cute girl, but as a man.

00:13:15.430 --> 00:13:16.310
Here I go!

00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:38.080
Murasame-san! Help me!

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:39.460
Akemiya-kun!

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:51.640
Murasame-san...

00:13:52.870 --> 00:13:53.800
It reeks!

00:13:57.230 --> 00:14:00.600
Murasame-san! Murasame-san!

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:03.620
That's cruel.

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:14.260
Just what are they doing?

00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:17.000
This is the next riddle.

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:18.970
A German?

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:22.010
Do we have one here?

00:14:22.010 --> 00:14:25.510
Even if there isn't one now,
there might have been one in the past.

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:28.030
Let's look for him, everyone.

00:14:35.550 --> 00:14:40.640
Wouldn't international students normally go to school in the city?

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:42.760
Hmm, you could be right.

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:47.070
German girls are really pretty.

00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:49.180
Their hair is so fluffy.

00:14:49.510 --> 00:14:52.320
We're looking for a guy, though.

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:55.540
Come to think of it,
it could even be a teacher.

00:15:01.220 --> 00:15:02.760
Murasame-san?

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:06.930
It's Aoi-san! Yahoo!

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:16.680
You do some strange things in the Girls' Club.

00:15:17.210 --> 00:15:20.330
We don't usually do things like this.

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:22.700
What did you come here to do, Aoi-san?

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:26.850
I thought I'd look for some reference material for the novel I'm going to write.

00:15:26.850 --> 00:15:29.630
Oh, what kind of novel is it?

00:15:29.630 --> 00:15:32.210
I haven't completely thought it out yet.

00:15:33.460 --> 00:15:36.000
But, you see...

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:39.580
Right now, I want to write about love.

00:15:40.110 --> 00:15:42.830
"Step back across the thorns," huh?

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:46.990
"Either way appeals to me."

00:15:49.290 --> 00:15:51.730
Would you let me read it once you're done?

00:15:52.400 --> 00:15:57.930
I'm interested in just what kind of conclusion you'll come to in the novel.

00:16:02.590 --> 00:16:06.730
Neither student nor teacher — he's not here.

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:12.480
Well, you don't come across a German every day.

00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:18.490
Here.

00:16:19.690 --> 00:16:22.750
What are you girls doing anyway?

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:26.700
We're not entirely sure ourselves.

00:16:26.700 --> 00:16:30.410
Akemiya was suffering in the infirmary.

00:16:30.410 --> 00:16:32.360
Don't do anything foolish.

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:37.480
Excuse me.

00:16:40.240 --> 00:16:43.680
I see. There are a lot of Germans here.

00:16:44.530 --> 00:16:48.340
Is it all right for us to touch the portraits?

00:16:49.410 --> 00:16:52.110
There shouldn't be a problem,
as long as we put them back afterwards.

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:55.290
First, let's round up the German composers.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:02.310
Well, there are other ones as well.

00:17:08.100 --> 00:17:11.420
I found it! Look, here it is!

00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:17.180
"If you seek it, don't forget your boots"?

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:20.770
Did someone take it home in the end?

00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:23.700
Well, we've come this far.

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:27.190
"Boots" is the key word here.

00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:32.460
For now, we should put back all the portraits except for Bach's.

00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:35.700
Yeah, you're right.

00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:42.660
Beethoven once said,

00:17:43.940 --> 00:17:47.600
"Bach is not a creek, but a sea."

00:17:48.530 --> 00:17:51.230
In German, "Bach" means "creek."

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:53.390
Creek...

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:55.610
In other words, here?

00:17:55.610 --> 00:17:56.880
Exactly.

00:17:57.100 --> 00:18:00.220
"That thing" must be here.

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:07.010
All right.

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:09.970
We'll wait until the rain subsides—

00:18:09.970 --> 00:18:12.370
What are you saying, Murasame-kun?

00:18:18.810 --> 00:18:22.770
So, we're going to dive in?
Right now? Just like that?

00:18:22.770 --> 00:18:25.950
The water isn't that deep, so we can't dive.

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:27.530
That's not the point!

00:18:27.530 --> 00:18:30.180
Can't we at least wait for
the rain to subside a little?

00:18:30.180 --> 00:18:34.530
No, we need to get to the bottom of this as quickly as possible.

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:37.510
If that's what Tomoe-chan wants, I'll do it!

00:18:37.890 --> 00:18:40.550
Kazama-kun and the others can wait here.

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:42.510
So it's decided that I have to?

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:46.270
Oh, I'll go! I love things like this!

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:52.520
Commencing upstream mission!

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:55.150
Let me know if you find anything!

00:18:57.810 --> 00:18:58.780
Sumi-chan!

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:02.780
It's more slippery than I thought.

00:19:03.190 --> 00:19:06.150
I'm all wet!

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:10.710
What are you doing?!

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:13.790
What? It's all your fault!

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:15.630
What are they doing?

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:17.800
Why are they in there?

00:19:22.920 --> 00:19:24.020
Come on.

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:33.060
Don't just stand there and laugh! Jump in!

00:19:41.420 --> 00:19:42.480
Here.

00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:55.340
Even though I told them
not to do anything foolish...

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:32.000
This isn't a river.

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:38.920
I found it!

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:45.490
I got the tickets.

00:20:45.490 --> 00:20:47.720
Give my regards to Mom and Dad.

00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:49.360
Sumika's looking forward to it as well!

00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:51.820
Thank goodness, it's cleared up.

00:20:53.750 --> 00:20:57.520
The last time I played in a river
was when I was still a child.

00:20:57.750 --> 00:21:00.730
I do it from time to time in the countryside,

00:21:01.250 --> 00:21:03.970
but this is the first time I've done it at school.

00:21:03.970 --> 00:21:07.180
The teacher told us to come see her in the office later.

00:21:08.850 --> 00:21:11.300
What was this all about anyway?

00:21:11.670 --> 00:21:14.510
It's just a prank, obviously.

00:21:18.640 --> 00:21:20.990
I don't think so.

00:21:22.330 --> 00:21:23.520
What do you mean?

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:28.480
We spent a lot of time after school,
yet we never got bored.

00:21:28.480 --> 00:21:30.300
On the contrary, we had fun.

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:36.030
Let's provide inquisitive underclassmen like ourselves with some entertainment.

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:41.740
I think that was the intention of the ones who first came up with this.

00:21:45.230 --> 00:21:48.530
Well then, it's our turn next.

00:21:52.990 --> 00:21:54.460
Where should we hide it?

00:23:31.140 --> 00:23:32.640
Ah, Kazama?

00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:36.390
Say...

00:23:47.200 --> 00:23:51.150
Ka-za-ma!
